## Prediction and rule of the pre-run entry

Prediction: the AR(1) residual keeps most of its power in band (share above 0.9) with r₁ near 0.75; the AR(p ≤ 5) residual's in-band share falls to about 0.5–0.6 (a mixture of flattened in-band noise at r₁ = 0.82 and amplified above-band residue at r₁ ≈ −0.4 has r₁ = 0.26 at an in-band share of 0.54); at p = 10 and 20 the share falls further toward 0.28 as r₁ approaches zero — the whitened series is increasingly the amplified stop-band residue. Rule: descriptive; quoted in the Remedies paragraph; no atoms are computed at p = 10 or 20. If the prediction fails (the AR(p) share stays above 0.9), the "amplified residue" explanation is dropped from the text and the remaining autocorrelation is reported without it.
